# Cloudflare Pages honours this file (unlike _redirects, see that file). One rule: the
# Atom feeds under /feeds/ are served as what they are, so a reader handed the URL
# recognises it without sniffing. scripts/build_feeds.py writes them.
/feeds/*
  Content-Type: application/atom+xml; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=900

# MARKDOWN AND RAW DATA ARE NOT SEARCH RESULTS.
#
# TJ, 27 September 2026: "people are finding markdown (from search?!) and saying 'I see
# code... I am overwhelmed'". They were: 147 of 967 sitemap URLs were raw .md and .csv,
# submitted to IndexNow on every run, so a resident searching for the town's athletics
# spending could land on a wall of pipes and hashes and conclude the site was broken.
#
# A markdown document is a SERVING FORMAT -- for the PDF renderer, for /docs, and for an
# agent that cannot run JavaScript. The same content exists as a designed page at
# /analysis/<id>, and that is what a person should be sent to.
#
# noindex, not a robots.txt block. The document stays fetchable, citable and hashed, so
# rule 12 is untouched and llms.txt can go on pointing agents straight at it. And removal
# of what is ALREADY indexed needs the crawler to fetch the URL and read this header --
# a disallowed URL is never re-read, so a noindex on it is never seen.
#
# The .md files under /docs/ get the same header from fy28/functions/docs/_bucket.js when
# they are served from the bucket rather than from disk. Both doors, one rule.
/*.md
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

/docs/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
